SBCL runtime options
====================

From a configured tree, run ./tests/sbcl-runtime-options.sh.  Automake also
runs it in make check when SBCL is enabled.  It needs a POSIX shell, the
configured SBCL executable, make, and the usual shell utilities; no Maxima image
is required.

The test independently probes --tls-limit support and checks that configure
substituted the detected setting.  It also executes the generated build
command, checking that runtime flags precede SBCL Lisp options.  It then runs the generated Unix launcher
with a recording runtime in both core and executable image layouts.  Sixteen
cases check the default limit, environment and command-line overrides, runtime
option ordering, and paths and Maxima arguments containing spaces.  The
configured default precedes user runtime options so an explicit limit wins.
A successful run exits zero and prints its case count; a mismatch exits
nonzero.  Temporary launchers and recordings are removed on exit.

The probe accepts older SBCL versions that reject --tls-limit: their generated
launchers must omit the unsupported default.  These tests exercise argument
forwarding and substitution rather than allocating thousands of Lisp symbols.
They do not execute the Windows batch launcher or test its command interpreter.
The same configured default is inserted before user options in both Windows
SBCL image layouts.
